1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,912
The Psychology of Procrastination.

2
00:00:02,862 --> 00:00:06,300
Procrastination is not a time management problem.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,100
It is an emotion regulation problem.

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:14,337
Tasks are avoided because they provoke anxiety, boredom, or overwhelm.

5
00:00:14,337 --> 00:00:19,050
The avoidance offers temporary relief but generates more stress over time.

6
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:23,650
The antidote is not better scheduling but reduction of the emotional barrier.

7
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:31,625
Breaking the task into the smallest possible first step — writing one sentence, opening one document — lowers resistance.

8
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:39,625
The Pomodoro technique, which structures work into focused 25-minute blocks with short breaks, makes commitments feel manageable.

9
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:42,250
Self-compassion also matters.

10
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:46,162
Berating oneself for procrastinating worsens the cycle.

11
00:00:46,162 --> 00:00:51,762
Acknowledging the avoidance, forgiving, and taking one small action is more effective.

